    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI'm working on a rust project and I noticed that I could not move between `@function` textobjects.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.4\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `nvim main.rs`\r\n3. Press `[f` or `]f`.\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Files\r\n[minimal.lua](https://dpaste.org/UsoQA)\r\n[main.rs](https://dpaste.org/BTKKS)\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nCursor should move to the previous/next function item.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nVerbose error is thrown.\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua: /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/query.lua:259: query: invalid structure at position 5163 for language rust\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function '_ts_parse_query'\r\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/query.lua:259: in function 'get_query'\r\n        ...r-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/shared.lua:99: in function 'available_textobjects'\r\n        ...r-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/shared.lua:83: in function 'get_query_strings_from_regex'\r\n        ...ter-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/move.lua:32: in function 'move_fn'\r\n        ...ects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/repeatable_move.lua:61: in function 'move_repeatable'\r\n        ...ter-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/move.lua:122: in function <...ter-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/move.lua:121>\r\n        ...r-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/attach.lua:45: in function <...r-textobjects/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/attach.lua:44>\r\n```",
